From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 14:40:10 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 97/97] Plutonium: DevTools on a Unix socket for this user only
 (--plutonium-remote-debugging-socket)

A --remote-debugging-port on 127.0.0.1 can be reached by every process on
the machine: other users, and sandboxed apps that share the host's network.
DevTools has no authentication, so any of them could drive the browser and
read its cookies and passwords. --plutonium-remote-debugging-socket=<path>
serves the same HTTP and WebSocket endpoints on a Unix socket instead, as
Chrome on Android does, and accepts only peers with this user's uid
(SO_PEERCRED). A stale socket at <path> is replaced.
---
 .../devtools/remote_debugging_server.cc       | 64 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 64 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/devtools/remote_debugging_server.cc b/chrome/browser/devtools/remote_debugging_server.cc
index 084c1427a6..607d0de454 100644
